course: dictionary
lesson: 10944
title: Waggle
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A waggle is a quick movement from side to side or up and down. «Waggle your fingers» means move your fingers quickly. The verb can also be waggles, waggled or waggling, and the noun a waggle is one small quick movement.
explain: Scientists use this word too. «A honeybee does a waggle dance in the hive; the angle and length of the dance tell other bees which way and how far to fly for food.» The waggle is the part of the dance where the bee shakes its body from side to side.
explain: Context helps again. In «The dog's tail gave a waggle», a tail is not a thing that can clap or shout, so a waggle must be a small movement. Ask yourself: what would the sentence look like if I put in my meaning? If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: To waggle means to move something quickly from side to side or up and down.
fact: Waggle can be a verb (waggle, waggles, waggled, waggling) or a noun (a waggle).
fact: «Give it a waggle» means move it gently from side to side, as with a loose tooth.
fact: In science, the honeybee's waggle dance shows other bees the direction and distance of flowers.
fact: Waggle is also used for playful movements of fingers, ears, eyebrows and tails.
exercise: «Waggle your fingers.» What does waggle mean here? | *Move them quickly from side to side | Put them in your pocket | Bend them tightly into a fist | Count them slowly
exercise: «The dog's tail gave a waggle.» What is a waggle here? | A long sleep | *A quick small movement | A loud bark | A wet nose
exercise: «A honeybee does a waggle dance in the hive; the angle and length of the dance tell other bees which way and how far to fly for food.» What is the dance for? | To make honey faster | To keep the hive warm | To scare away enemies | *To show other bees where the food is
test: Dad waggles his eyebrows to make us laugh. What does waggles mean? | Shuts them tightly | Counts them | *Moves them quickly up and down | Paints them red
test: Lily says her loose tooth needs a waggle. What does she mean? | Eat something hard | *Move it gently from side to side | Pull it out with pliers | Ask the dentist for help
exam: The bee was ___ its body to show the way to the flowers. Which form fits best? | waggly | waggles | waggler | *waggling
